<!--
  /reference — the per-directive + runtime-API cheat sheet. Every construct is
  verified against the in-repo sui-compiler. Syntax lives in codeblocks (strings)
  so braces read as text, not template expressions.
-->
<div class="doc">
  <p class="eyebrow">Reference</p>
  <h1>Reference</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Every directive, binding, and runtime primitive in one place. Each entry is
    verified against the compiler — if it's here, it compiles.
  </p>

  <h2>Text &amp; expressions</h2>
  <p>Read a signal or any JavaScript expression directly in the markup.</p>
  <sui-codeblock code={code.text}></sui-codeblock>

  <h2>Events</h2>
  <p>
    Bind any DOM event with <code>on:</code>; chain modifiers to declare intent
    instead of writing the boilerplate by hand.
  </p>
  <sui-codeblock code={code.events}></sui-codeblock>

  <h2>Bindings &amp; refs</h2>
  <p>
    Two-way binding keeps a form control and a signal in sync;
    <code>bind:this</code> hands you the element itself via a
    <code>ref()</code>.
  </p>
  <sui-codeblock code={code.bind}></sui-codeblock>

  <h2>Class, style &amp; props</h2>
  <p>Conditional classes, CSS custom properties, and passing props to a child.</p>
  <sui-codeblock code={code.attrs}></sui-codeblock>

  <h2>Control flow</h2>
  <p>
    Conditionals, keyed loops, and discriminated matches. Each is a partial — it
    splices into the surrounding markup with no wrapper element. The
    <code>key</code> on a loop is required for stable reorders.
  </p>
  <sui-codeblock code={code.controlFlow}></sui-codeblock>

  <h2>Async &amp; live data</h2>
  <p>
    Render the loading, error, and loaded states of a <code>live()</code> or
    <code>data live</code> handle. The loaded value is only reachable through
    <code>kind === 'ok'</code>, so a template can't render data it hasn't
    confirmed arrived.
  </p>
  <sui-codeblock code={code.asyncData}></sui-codeblock>

  <h2>Runtime API</h2>
  <p>The reactive primitives, imported from <code>@ship/sui-runtime</code>.</p>
  <sui-codeblock code={code.runtime}></sui-codeblock>

  <h2>Declarations</h2>
  <p>
    Props, scoped styles, and live server data — the file-level declarations at
    the top of a <code>.sui</code>. Reactive logic lives in the paired
    <code>.controller.ts</code>.
  </p>
  <sui-codeblock code={code.declarations}></sui-codeblock>

  <h2>Slots</h2>
  <p>Named and default content wells — the composition seam.</p>
  <sui-codeblock code={code.slots}></sui-codeblock>

  <div class="page-nav">
    <a class="btn" href="/tooling">← Tooling</a>
    <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/components">Component library →</a>
  </div>
</div>
